"""IT28 2026-11-28: SCI's ADV-295 block 2 (DL-MECH-170, S1-S3) and ADV-297 (I1, I2, I4, I5) as exact-once fragment replacements in the discovery ledger. I3 (CLAIM 024) is NOT applied (reason in RESULT). Hypothesis level; nothing here is medical advice."""
LED = "disease-models/wwox/research/discovery_ledger_current.md"
X = []
def f(path, old, new, tag): X.append(dict(path=path, old=old, new=new, tag=tag))
f(LED, "**Symptomatic in every paper that looks.** Genotype decides whether a T-type block is mechanism-matched: gain-of-function T-type variants cause seizures and loss-of-function variants cause neurodevelopmental disease without seizures (PMID 33704440, PMID 40825030).",
 "**Carrier phenotype does not settle direction.** Whether a T-type block opposes the defect depends on the measured direction of the individual variant, not on whether the carrier has seizures (our inference; no cited paper tests a blocker on a variant channel, though PMID 33704440 reports one clinical case, an I860N carrier, whose seizure control improved on ethosuximide). In CACNA1I (Cav3.3), four variants classed gain-of-function in transfected HEK293T cells were found in six individuals with neurodevelopmental phenotypes; two carriers (aged 28 and 31 years in the main text; their seizure status is from Supplementary Table S1, which the blind reader did not hold) are recorded without seizures, while a third carrier developed late-onset seizures at 58 years (PMID 33704440). A second series reports a partial loss-of-function variant (p.Ala398Val) in two unrelated children, aged 13 and 4 years, without seizures so far, and a gain-of-function carrier (M1425V, 25 years) without documented seizures but with lifelong staring spells; its authors write that both gain- and loss-of-function variants can cause neurodevelopmental disease (PMID 40825030). Neither supports a rule for T-type channels as a class.", "S1")
f(LED, "The T-type change is lesion-specific in sign and age (an increase in Cntnap2, PMID 40834072; a decrease under developmental oxidative stress, PMID 35079122).",
 "Across separate studies (not a matched comparison), the thalamic reticular low-threshold (T-type) current density differs in sign between mouse models: higher in Cntnap2 knockout (net inward current, T-type-attributed but not isolated; adult males, 8 to 14 weeks; PMID 40834072, targeted search only), lower in redox or neurodevelopmental models (PMID 35079122: germline Gclm knockout at postnatal day 60 to 75 but not day 20 to 30; at day 20 to 30 only after an added early-life challenge or prenatal MAM, as a decrease across prepulse potentials that is not significant at resting potential; ex vivo, neuron-level statistics).", "S2")
f(LED, "a Neuroligin 2 line (PMID 32719346) shows a restriction that follows the SWD phenotype (no effect in wild type or in two non-SWD mutants);",
 "in a Neuroligin 2 knockout with spike-wave discharges, ethosuximide (200 mg/kg intraperitoneal, before/after; no vehicle arm for the behavioural tests in the main text) partially improved behaviour; in wild-type mice it had no effect on locomotion, anxiety-like behaviour or social recognition memory, and the social-memory deficit was not rescued in PAK3-transgenic mice (no seizures, by citation) or FMR1-knockout mice (increased susceptibility to non-absence seizures, by citation); whether those lines have absence-type discharges was not recorded in the main text; the pattern is consistent with, and does not prove, an action that depends on the discharges (the authors' own caution); in thalamic slices of wild-type and knockout mice ethosuximide 500 uM reduced the number of action potentials in the rebound burst (PMID 32719346);", "S3")
f(LED, "la mappa del sito attivo SDR di WWOX è S260 (substrato), **S281 + motivo YxxxK Y293–K297** (catalisi), motivo Rossmann GxxxGxG N-terminale per NAD ([struttura, PMC4374002](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4374002/))",
 "the SDR active-site map of WWOX is a sequence-and-model assignment, not an experimental structure: S260 (substrate), the Y293/K297 dyad of the YxxxK motif, and GxxxGxG for the NADP(H) cofactor (review, PMID 25662954 / [PMC4374002](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4374002/)); a serine 12 residues upstream of the YNRSK motif (about position 281 by count; no residue number is given) and a «NAD(H) or NADP(H)» site GANSGIG 131-137 are reported from sequence analysis in PMID 21476439, and that serine is not the review's S260 [correction dated 2026-11-28: the earlier text attributed S281 and NAD to PMC4374002 and called the map a «structure»]", "I1")
f(LED, "- WW1 **nel modulo tandem** lega **2-3× più forte** che da solo, con **guadagno entropico**.",
 "- WW1 **nel modulo tandem** lega **2-3× più forte** che da solo, con **guadagno entropico**.\n- Review PMID 25662954 (same laboratory; Table 1; ITC, 25 °C, pH 7, at least three measurements) gives, for eight 12-residue PPPY peptides, a WW1-WW2 gain over WW1 alone of 1.8- to 5.1-fold (p73 1.8; ErbB4 2.4; TMG2 2.4; WBP1 2.6; WBP2 3.2; PTCH1 3.5; PTPN14 3.6; SMAD7 5.1); the folds are ratios of the Table 1 values (the review prints no per-ligand fold); the review's text says «two- to threefold», which four ligands exceed (WBP2 3.2, PTCH1 3.5, PTPN14 3.6, SMAD7 5.1) and p73 (1.8) falls below. The rows for p73, PTCH1, PTPN14, SMAD7 and TMG2 are stated there as unpublished.", "I2")
f(LED, "`IPOTESI`, non misurata in questo paper in alcuna forma.",
 "`IPOTESI`, non misurata in questo paper in alcuna forma.\n- In vitro, a 12-residue SMAD7 PPPY peptide (LESPPPPYSRYP; not full-length SMAD7) binds WW1 with Kd 272 ± 29 µM and the WW1-WW2 tandem with 53 ± 8 µM (ITC, 25 °C, pH 7, mean ± 1 SD, at least three measurements; PMID 25662954, Table 1; the row is stated as unpublished in the 2015 review). Competition with Smurf and the effect on Smad4 remain unmeasured.", "I4")
f(LED, "the corpus's SDR reading has rested on one laboratory's crude-extract enzymology.",
 "the corpus's SDR reading has rested on one laboratory's crude-extract enzymology (a 2015 review, PMID 25662954, states, as preliminary and without data, rate, constant or construct, that a bacterially purified recombinant SDR domain appears to interconvert retinol and retinal, while PMID 21476439 reports that the oxidoreductase activity was lost on purification; neither statement is used here as a substrate or binder).", "I5")
